Audit synthesis 2026-09-12 (CC-AUDIT-SKIN-20260912-1D83F0A4, CC-AUDIT-20260912-7A5E0C31 F-05): mandatory diagnosis protocol before any weight/radius tuning. The audit is explicit that the same "untouched limb moves" symptom can originate from wrong influence classification, an over-broad Body influence radius, wrong pose rotation, wrong bindpose, actor/world-space mismatch, or a debug visualisation using the wrong coordinate space. Do not infer a weight bug from screenshots or source inspection.

Required experiment on a real generated creature:
1. capture the top four influences for every affected vertex;
2. visualise the dominant influence;
3. pose one non-leg Body bone at a time;
4. compare untouched-leg vertex displacement;
5. compare the pure LBS oracle against the actual SMR result;
6. classify the fault, then tune.

Also note: a debug/visualisation tool must be validated against a posed, non-identity state before it is trusted as evidence for diagnosing a different bug (RigDebugView mixed rest-space and posed-space coordinates in an earlier round).

Ownership separation to preserve: TSK-0150 is the foot/domain isolation mechanism; this task is the untouched-limb deformation mechanism. The audit explicitly says these must not be folded together. Related: TSK-0172 (body smear), TSK-0194 (LBS parity failure cluster D).
